Welcome back, everyone is Charlie.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.853
This will be my For Last of Us
Episode 2 video.

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:22.622
There's a whole bunch easter eggs and
references, so we'll break it all down.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:25.492
If you're brand new to the channel,
I'm doing videos for all the episodes.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:27.460
Be sure to subscribe to get them all.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.263
We're also doing a giveaway
for HBO Max subscriptions.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.265
All you have to do to enter
is be a subscriber

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:35.402
and just push your favorite moment
from the episode on the video.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:37.837
Careful for spoilers
if you haven't seen the episode yet,

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.873
we'll just start at the beginning, work
our way through, shot by shot.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:44.010
Talking about Easter eggs in WTF moments,
starting with the title of the episode.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.279
It was Infected,
which is literally a reference

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:50.350
to all the people who have been infected
in the origin of the cordyceps fungus.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:54.020
This episode was another history lesson
in a tutorial in present day

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:57.090
about how the fungus just works
in general, like where it came from, how

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.627
it started confirming a bunch of theories
that episode one.

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:03.029
Turns out flour is the real villain here,

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:04.798
but in present day
there are a lot of references

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:08.234
to how the fungus works on the infected
and different types of infected.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.737
Like we finally see some clickers up
close and personal.

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:14.174
The actual opening scene starts
in another flashback to life in Jakarta,

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:18.178
Indonesia in 2003, right before Joel
and his daughter in episode

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:21.181
one heard the news about problems
there on the radio.

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.283
The main reason why the fungus hit here
first

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:27.087
is because of the warmer average climate
and because of the flower.

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:30.690
Jakarta holds the world's
largest flower factory.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.793
The whole idea is that the fungus had an
easier time surviving in warmer climates.

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:37.363
So as global warming slowly increase,
the average temperatures around the world,

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.332
like certain places in the world,
were just warmer

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.734
naturally than others, Jakarta
being one of them.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.904
And because they had the largest
flower plant there, it just natural that

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:47.907
that's where the first giant outbreak
of the fungus was.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:51.277
And remember, it's the mutant fungus
because the woman who investigates

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.413
it is like,
Oh no, it can never survive in humans.

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:54.747
We don't have to worry about it.

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.583
The military men come to pick her up.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:02:00.320
She's a professor of mycology,
which is the study of fungus.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:04.023
They want to develop a vaccine, but
turns out there is no actual cure for it.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:04.591
Like Elly

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:08.194
is meant to be the first known person
in the series in the games who's immune.

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:10.997
That's why they're trying to use her
to create a vaccine.

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:14.501
The version of the fungus that she winds
up looking at here is the mutated version

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:18.037
because the sample was taken from a human
and they show you how they discovered

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.339
the first known infected,

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:22.375
at least that they know of in
how they try to get more information.

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:23.977
I love the way that some of this plays
out, too.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.478
Like the guard tells her,
If you feel sick,

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:29.082
be sure you leave this room, which is like
the worst possible thing she could do.

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:30.517
Like,
that's just another way to spread it.

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:32.318
But that's when they had spores in there.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.521
Not really doing spores during season one.

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:37.190
The showrunner said that they might do
spores in season two, so, like,

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:40.093
they still might be a thing
and they reference spores in present day

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:42.495
when Ellie is talking
about the different types of infected.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:45.365
So the main way to get infected right now
is just to get bitten

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:47.033
by one of the other infected.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:47.901
So as long as the woman

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:51.738
didn't get infected here or the fungus
didn't get inside her suit, she'd be fine.

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.840
The bullet wound in her head
was where they shot her,

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.642
because, as they said, she turned violent.

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:56.776
She turned into a runner.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:57.510
Basically,

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.413
all the things they're describing,
the stuff that we saw during episode one.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.215
So, like we've already seen this play out.

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:05.151
It is possible to kill the infected,
but as the fungus progresses

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:06.819
through different stages,
it creates stronger

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:09.756
and stronger armor around their bodies
and they gain the ability to spit

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:13.159
acid, throw spore bombs,
which they reference later in the episode.

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:16.629
So there aren't super infected
fungal spores on you,

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:19.832
or ones with split open heads
that see in the dark like bats.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:22.502
Hopefully they're not infected
through spore bombs at you.

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:24.871
Boy, is Ellie
going to be in for a surprise.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:27.240
But the big idea here
is that they got her with the head shot,

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.441
which is how you kill them.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.577
It's just like on The Walking Dead
with the walkers.

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:33.146
You get them with a head shot,
That's how you take them down.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:35.815
You also notice that when she discovers
the fungus in her mouth,

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.450
it's still growing, which they reference.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.919
Later in the episode
to look. The fungus continues on.

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:41.621
Even if you've killed the infected,

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:44.023
which in the games
is another reference to the spores.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.692
Like the whole idea
that when you kill someone,

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:48.528
they give off spores
and they can continue to infect you.

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:50.029
So that's why the infected on

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:54.133
the last of us are way more dangerous
than the walkers on The Walking Dead.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.001
The whole thing here is then

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:59.272
just confirming where the first infected
were found in a flower grain factory.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:01.975
Also supporting the flower theory
from episode one.

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:04.711
There's a type of fungus
that just naturally grows around.

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:07.914
Grain isn't harmful to humans by the time
it makes it through flour mills

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:09.449
and into food products.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:11.985
During episode one,
there were all these references to Joel

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:12.752
and his daughter

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:16.089
not eating flour because they were like
they didn't have any flour in.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.390
Somehow they survived.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.492
They didn't get infected
like their neighbors

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:21.794
who were eating cookies
with flour in them.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:24.030
Also, the world's
largest flour mill is in Jakarta.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:24.831
So it's just the show

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:28.835
saying that the origin of the fungus
was Jakarta in the flour here.

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:31.671
It was the perfect quote
unquote substrate, as she says.

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:33.840
But the factory here
where they had this initial outbreak,

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:37.577
they cut 14 people and claimed
that there's one person that they missed,

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:41.648
the person that bit her, the 15th person,
which is how it spread around the city.

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:44.517
And then it cuts to the scene
where she basically tells them

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:47.487
that there is no possibility for a vaccine
or a cure.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.588
The best way to take care of

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:52.759
this would be to bomb the city, kill
everybody in it, and hope to contain it.

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:55.061
But there's another reference
to this later in the episode

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:57.063
when Taz talks about
what happened to Boston,

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:59.565
about how they bombed
all the cities in the U.S.

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:03.069
as a way to do the same thing,
to try and contain the fungus.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:06.406
I couldn't detect any changes
to the opening credits from episode one.

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:10.710
It is the same theme song from the games
like The Last of US main theme song.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:14.113
I reference this during my episode
one video, but the growth inside

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:18.184
the opening credits is the fungus
growing in the map of the United States

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:20.320
and then the rest of the world
spreading around the world.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.789
Like you can see
the outline of the United States here.

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:25.892
You can also see Joel and Ellie's
outline in here, too.

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:27.994
Then in present day,
we pick up with Joel and Tess

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:30.196
watching over
Ellie as she sleeps and wakes up.

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:32.865
The reason why he has the gun on her
is that he's still worried

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:35.435
that she's going to turn
and try to bite them, infect them,

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:37.203
because it takes them a while
to come around.

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:38.771
It's not till the end of the episode
when he starts

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:41.140
to actually believe
that she might be immune.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:44.010
Pretty much this entire episode,
at least the present day of the episode,

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:47.347
is taken directly from the games,
but it's like a much more elongated

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:50.616
version, like it's much more stretched out
version of this part of the game

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:51.250
with him trying to

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:55.021
make it across the downtown district
to get her to the other fireflies.

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:57.924
So they basically start from square
one here with this whole scene of her

00:05:57.924 --> 00:06:01.561
explaining everything to them about how
she's immune, teasing her backstory

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:04.764
a little bit with Marlene about how
she found her after she'd been infected.

00:06:04.764 --> 00:06:06.232
They'll be more flashbacks for this

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:10.069
and future episodes for Ellie's backstory
with Riley, with her mother.

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:12.572
She also makes a few references
to this later in the episode to

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:15.575
when she starts talking about
how she got bitten in the first place.

00:06:15.575 --> 00:06:18.411
The whole joke with the chicken sandwich
is that the rations in

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:22.048
the city are generally terrible
and never enough to meet people's needs,

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:24.851
so they rely on smugglers
to bring in food to the city,

00:06:24.851 --> 00:06:26.719
which is how the fireflies
got the chicken.

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:30.223
But Joel and Tess are smugglers,
like they're the people responsible

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:30.923
for doing that.

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:33.426
But they're stuck eating
this really terrible jerky.

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:35.161
There's a lot of scenes
early on here, too,

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:38.231
where Ellie tries to cut the tension
by telling inappropriate

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:41.067
jokes like, Don't do that. Don't
pretend you're infected.

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:44.070
Just to show you how she's going
to balance out the relationship with Joel

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:47.373
like Joel is this super serious person
in the relationship.

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:49.008
Ellie is the person that,
at least at first

00:06:49.008 --> 00:06:50.576
they'll use for a lot of comedic relief.

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:52.612
But she's also a very tragic character.

00:06:52.712 --> 00:06:56.282
So this is you know, any time she gets
really serious, shit is about to go down.

00:06:56.282 --> 00:07:00.153
Not expecting Joel to start telling jokes
any time soon.

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:03.756
The way that Joel talks about the idea
of a vaccine in the Fireflies

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:05.825
working out west in Salt Lake City,
sounds like

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:09.061
it's been an urban myth for a long time,
and he just doesn't believe it yet

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:12.598
because, as Tess says, for now at least,
this part of the episode,

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:14.967
they still really don't care about her
that much.

00:07:14.967 --> 00:07:15.768
They're only doing this

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:17.670
so they can get the reward
from the fireflies,

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:21.007
and he can get to his brother
in Wyoming to make sure that is okay.

00:07:21.007 --> 00:07:23.209
In a lot of these scenes here
where you get tutorials

00:07:23.209 --> 00:07:25.678
on how the fungus works,
how the different infected

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:28.114
work are meant to be viewed
from Ellie's perspective.

00:07:28.114 --> 00:07:29.916
Because even though she knows
a lot of this stuff,

00:07:29.916 --> 00:07:31.951
she's seeing all this for the first time.

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:35.822
I love the wide shot around the destroyed
area of Boston here, too.

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:37.423
Really great special effects.

00:07:37.423 --> 00:07:40.026
Like I said, when Tess starts
talking about the bombing of cities,

00:07:40.026 --> 00:07:42.528
it's another reference to the beginning
of the episode where the woman is like,

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:44.630
the only way to contain
this would be for you to bomb

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:48.100
this entire city and kill everybody
in it, as Tess is talking about it.

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:51.204
And they're staring in this giant
bomb crater, you know, is the car

00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:55.575
that they pass is an early 2000s model
because that's when the city was bombed.

00:07:55.575 --> 00:07:57.810
The mall that Ellie talks about,
where she was a bit

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:01.681
is more of her backstory with Riley
that they'll cover in future episodes.

00:08:01.681 --> 00:08:03.483
They might change the way
this works on the show

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:05.251
just a little to make it more tragic.

00:08:05.251 --> 00:08:06.452
But originally in the games,

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:09.222
Ellie was bit by a runner
as they were trying to escape.

00:08:09.222 --> 00:08:12.859
They might say on the show that she was
bit by Riley after she had turned just

00:08:12.859 --> 00:08:17.129
to make circumstances of her backstory
even more tragic than they already are.

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:21.000
She's lying to test when she says she was
alone inside the mall when she was bit.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:24.871
She was with Riley, who got bit
and she was forced to kill her, kill her

00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:25.838
best friend.

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:28.207
When she says she's an orphan,
her mother is going to be played

00:08:28.207 --> 00:08:30.776
by Ashley Johnson,
who was the voice of Ellie in the games,

00:08:30.776 --> 00:08:32.345
who will be featured in flashbacks

00:08:32.345 --> 00:08:35.014
in future episodes
when they do more of her backstory.

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:37.483
There's another big video game reference
and more foreshadowing

00:08:37.483 --> 00:08:39.886
for the future types of infected
they'll encounter

00:08:40.019 --> 00:08:43.289
when she starts joking about infected
that shoots spores at you.

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:47.093
Those are a reference to blotters, which
are like the fourth stage of the fungus.

00:08:47.093 --> 00:08:49.395
They're like very advanced
versions of the fungus.

00:08:49.395 --> 00:08:50.596
You start out as a runner,

00:08:50.596 --> 00:08:52.632
then you turn into a shamble
after a little while,

00:08:52.632 --> 00:08:55.201
then you turn into a clicker,
which we see later in the episode.

00:08:55.301 --> 00:08:59.238
And then after a bunch more time,
you evolve into a blotter in addition

00:08:59.238 --> 00:09:02.642
to the spore bombs,
the blotters also have super tough skin,

00:09:02.642 --> 00:09:06.345
so they're way harder to kill than runners
shamblers or clickers.

00:09:06.345 --> 00:09:08.848
The ones with the split open heads
that have echolocation

00:09:08.848 --> 00:09:12.018
like bats, as she says, are the clickers
that we see in the episode,

00:09:12.018 --> 00:09:15.221
which is also where we hear that
first cry of the episode like up.

00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:15.821
Yet they are.

00:09:15.821 --> 00:09:18.424
We're going to see them in a little while
when they make it in the hotel

00:09:18.424 --> 00:09:20.760
and Alex starts
playing around making all that noise.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:23.162
Obviously very bad.
Don't want to make a bunch of noise.

00:09:23.162 --> 00:09:26.832
They have another perfect copy of a scene
that was taken from the video games

00:09:26.832 --> 00:09:29.468
when she's joking about
checking into the hotel.

00:09:30.202 --> 00:09:30.770
Yes, sir.

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:32.905
I would like your finest suite, please.

00:09:32.905 --> 00:09:36.542
Oh, I'll be checking in for one night,
and I would like your finest suite.

00:09:36.542 --> 00:09:39.145
Please help you doing?

00:09:39.145 --> 00:09:39.979
Why, yes.

00:09:39.979 --> 00:09:42.582
You can take my luggage upstairs.

00:09:42.582 --> 00:09:44.383
You are a weird kid.

00:09:44.383 --> 00:09:46.752
And weird kid. You're a weird kid.

00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:50.356
But you notice when Joel helps her up,
he recoils his hand

00:09:50.356 --> 00:09:52.692
because he's still not 100% on
being immune.

00:09:52.692 --> 00:09:54.226
He's still worried about getting infected.

00:09:54.226 --> 00:09:55.795
Like you can't touch her too much.

00:09:55.795 --> 00:09:56.762
The switchblade night

00:09:56.762 --> 00:10:00.733
that she has, which he compliments
her on, was given to her by Marlene.

00:10:00.733 --> 00:10:04.470
We'll see Marlene again on the show like
she's a pretty big character in the story.

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:07.440
She gets a little bit more of a tutorial
about how the infected live,

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:09.775
like some of them
live a little bit longer than others.

00:10:09.775 --> 00:10:13.145
That's just a reference to them
evolving into higher states

00:10:13.145 --> 00:10:15.781
like the clickers,
which we see pretty shortly,

00:10:15.781 --> 00:10:18.451
like the idea
that some of them live longer, 20

00:10:18.451 --> 00:10:21.487
plus years, even without other people
trying to kill them,

00:10:21.487 --> 00:10:24.423
they just naturally continue
to evolve their whole back

00:10:24.423 --> 00:10:27.093
and forth here to where they start
talking to each other about their past.

00:10:27.093 --> 00:10:30.096
Like, have you ever killed anyone who's
been infected, who used to be a person?

00:10:30.096 --> 00:10:31.297
How did you feel about that?

00:10:31.297 --> 00:10:35.267
That's her slowly opening up
in trying to talk more about what happened

00:10:35.267 --> 00:10:38.704
with her and Riley in her backstory,
because it's still very traumatic for her.

00:10:38.704 --> 00:10:41.440
But Joel, at this point doesn't
want to have anything to do with it.

00:10:41.507 --> 00:10:43.709
He doesn't want to examine his past
at all.

00:10:43.709 --> 00:10:46.212
He wants to tamp that down
as much as possible.

00:10:46.212 --> 00:10:49.715
The whole idea is he's been so traumatized
in his past that he just wants to forget

00:10:49.715 --> 00:10:52.952
about all of that pain, just push it down,
which is why at the end of the episode

00:10:52.952 --> 00:10:54.153
is so heartbreaking for him,

00:10:54.153 --> 00:10:58.224
